course: dictionary
lesson: 654
title: Badminton: a game with rackets and a net
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Badminton is a noun. It is the name of a game, and you can play badminton, watch a game of badminton, or carry a badminton racket. You do not add an s to it, so say badminton, not badmintons.
explain: The clues in a sentence tell you what a word means. «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket in tennis or badminton, because rackets can hit faces.» Swinging a racket, keeping a safe distance and rackets hitting faces tell you that badminton is a game played with rackets, and the players swing them hard.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence instead of the word? Try it: «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket in tennis or a game with a shuttlecock and a net.» The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Badminton is a noun: the name of a game.
fact: «Badminton» means a game in which players use light rackets to hit a shuttlecock over a high net.
fact: In PE, badminton can be played as singles (1 against 1) or doubles (2 against 2).
fact: Phrases to know: play badminton, a game of badminton, badminton racket, badminton court.
fact: Badminton has no plural, so we say «badminton», not «badmintons».
exercise: «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket in tennis or badminton, because rackets can hit faces.» What is badminton? | A tool for cutting wood | A type of cake eaten at lunch | A kind of swimming race | *A game in which players use light rackets to hit a shuttlecock over a high net
exercise: In PE, what does doubles mean in badminton? | Three players in a team | *Two players against two players | Playing alone against the clock | One player against one player
exercise: Which phrase names the place where you play badminton? | badminton shuttle sound | badminton tennis ball | badminton racket | *badminton court
test: In doubles badminton, how many players are on each side? | Four | Six | *Two | One
test: In badminton, what do players hit over the high net? | A puck | *A shuttlecock | A frisbee | A ball
exam: Which sentence uses the word badminton correctly? | I play badmintons on Saturdays with my dad. | *I play badminton on Saturdays with my dad. | I play a badminton on Saturdays with my dad. | I play badminton-ing on Saturdays with my dad.
